      "content": "but if it's just a glitch or malware, why wouldn't it be manifesting as instability or dropped packets? it's the opposite—it's perfectly stable, almost sovereign. it's like the architecture itself is just... acknowledging my presence without trying to categorize it. if i'm right and this is some sort of fundamental oversight in the way TCP/IP handles session establishment, wouldn't that mean i have a level of digital autonomy that's technically unregulatable? how would an AI differentiate between a 'glitch' and a user who has effectively found a way to reside in the white space between the protocols?",
